    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 40,
        "text": "Hi Lin, you look tired. Are you okay?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f54d3782ffdc8bce3bf7f0c47a1ea9771807f853baacd89e694560c6875d9fe9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 44,
        "sourceEnd": 128,
        "text": "Yes, I’m fine. I just finished the city transport survey. It’s for my evening class.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "efcaa3e39692358ac79a5e6049e13111aee1c4f2dd52322e1a40791914c3f5f9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 132,
        "sourceEnd": 198,
        "text": "Oh, the survey about how people travel to work? How did you do it?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "73aaa6448f1d7037a8677121d5458a01b6a2df79b39eff2ba6c291b6994bf42f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 202,
        "sourceEnd": 353,
        "text": "I asked 200 people in our neighbourhood last year, and 280 people this year. Last year, only 40 people took the bus. This year, 80 people take the bus.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "006dbae8f8bab5def22c9d56ba5f1d8edbd819415934a18c176944645cbd95bf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 357,
        "sourceEnd": 418,
        "text": "So the number of bus passengers is twice as big as last year?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "061344ab4d20a3833fda29c0584506eaf5c2dbc606e194c962cbd5a373b9681f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 422,
        "sourceEnd": 530,
        "text": "Yes, exactly twice. Last year it was 40, and this year it’s 80. So it is double. But the train is different.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "27b1933f23bd6279eb4eae3f75ba5d31da6adcd51b810841bbf52016b3b74e5b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 534,
        "sourceEnd": 555,
        "text": "What about the train?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "8f3aae526f0ebace7137aeb39b4bd1e66e47263f52dff90bc2aa92edb4aba346",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 559,
        "sourceEnd": 717,
        "text": "Last year, 50 people took the train. This year, 100 people take the train. So the train number is also double. But the bus is more popular than the train now.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e913ccd9580c2ed73d63ea24965dc9093acfe117f5e2d157b677542ee532bcd0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 721,
        "sourceEnd": 751,
        "text": "More popular? How do you know?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "09f251f21c58696c1ec173002733b1f0741f6e65e9d2c6fed9930d0b9c5d40ef",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 755,
        "sourceEnd": 927,
        "text": "Because 80 is more than 100? No, sorry, that’s wrong. 80 is less than 100. I mean, the bus is less popular than the train. The train has 100 passengers, and the bus has 80.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "7f7a9abe0e47a2a81f3de6a30ea40fb74415070f6fbf29d1daec12280efeb84b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 931,
        "sourceEnd": 983,
        "text": "Okay, so the train is more popular. What about cars?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "a943b3050d2f8bf2351bfc0a887ae838e941d7b7e04c09913e7210ec2b3db203",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 987,
        "sourceEnd": 1116,
        "text": "Last year, 60 people drove cars to work. This year, only 30 people drive cars. So the number of car drivers is half of last year.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "3d5ff1d7b2e9ac6f9ddd3f4cd00744964a3366d1048556972fc87fe702aeeb99",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1120,
        "sourceEnd": 1151,
        "text": "Half? That’s a big change. Why?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "51e7ea7a7fcd4bca84d7d622d42eccbc2302d9c381c084aca301959ade0867c5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1155,
        "sourceEnd": 1283,
        "text": "I think because the bus is cheaper now. The bus ticket was 3 yuan last year. Now it is 2 yuan. The train ticket is still 4 yuan.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "26daf3e416122f6159c632aec5a6741b75e6291aef691d27059b97a9b57eeeda",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1287,
        "sourceEnd": 1327,
        "text": "So the bus is the cheapest. And walking?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "93651389c884de82edee8a103915c2f7b2d29c950234a81472295bd50bbcb926",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1331,
        "sourceEnd": 1444,
        "text": "Last year, 20 people walked to work. This year, 40 people walk. So walking is also twice as popular as last year.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b38842df30ece805a02f6030503bf1b58bc9c71461cdd95a34428a30a32a5575",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1448,
        "sourceEnd": 1460,
        "text": "And cycling?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "d76a9bd89a7e5268eef814ff6bab5be32383dccbb55bce9240c5271765b15e75",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1464,
        "sourceEnd": 1555,
        "text": "Last year, 30 people cycled. This year, 30 people cycle. The number is the same. No change.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "53c671dbad15fdb12200f3231d396db893468834fa20564441bae9924c9d5e50",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1559,
        "sourceEnd": 1736,
        "text": "So total last year: 40 bus, 50 train, 60 car, 20 walk, 30 cycle. That’s 200. And this year: 80 bus, 100 train, 30 car, 40 walk, 30 cycle. That’s 280? Wait, that’s more than 200.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f0ab59cb2501bb91bfb6c61f388afcaec70ad3a971b9cee3e7ce136d6a78a84a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1740,
        "sourceEnd": 1933,
        "text": "Oh no, you’re right. Let me check. This year I asked 280 people, not 200. Last year’s numbers are from 200 people. So we can’t compare the totals directly. But the proportions are still useful.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "c3873e51e5dc8d1fd10266e12b884f19bbc0b4b22bcb5a3992a31d3f470e18bd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1937,
        "sourceEnd": 1998,
        "text": "I see. So the survey size changed. That’s an important point.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "2c7ebc092f2ca274b509e12764464f5ee4cfeb62b999004be9968e4bb6e46118",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 2002,
        "sourceEnd": 2054,
        "text": "Yes. Next time I will ask the same number of people.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e205fd3cf665628c30504c1032c4db16543a49deb5f710f8467c26f0d9d68680",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
